WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.501
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book two.

2
00:00:05.801 --> 00:00:09.733
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:15.658
Unit eleven: Music Around the World. In this unit, you will talk about different kinds of music.

4
00:00:16.650 --> 00:00:17.430
Music.

5
00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:21.883
Music means sounds that are pleasant, made by singing or instruments.

6
00:00:22.183 --> 00:00:23.730
Music makes me happy.

7
00:00:24.430 --> 00:00:27.140
Your turn. Say: Music.

8
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.714
Music.

9
00:00:31.717 --> 00:00:32.590
Instrument.

10
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:35.893
Instrument means an object used to make music.

11
00:00:36.193 --> 00:00:38.204
The guitar is my favourite instrument.

12
00:00:38.904 --> 00:00:41.313
Your turn. Say: Instrument.

13
00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:45.084
Instrument.

14
00:00:46.083 --> 00:00:47.026
Traditional.

15
00:00:47.726 --> 00:00:50.190
Traditional means from a culture's long history.

16
00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:52.443
We learn traditional Khmer music.

17
00:00:53.143 --> 00:00:55.796
Your turn. Say: Traditional.

18
00:00:58.496 --> 00:00:59.497
Traditional.

19
00:01:00.483 --> 00:01:01.299
Band.

20
00:01:01.999 --> 00:01:05.124
Band means a group of people who play music together.

21
00:01:05.424 --> 00:01:07.018
My brother plays in a band.

22
00:01:07.718 --> 00:01:10.126
Your turn. Say: Band.

23
00:01:12.826 --> 00:01:13.537
Band.

24
00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:15.261
Concert.

25
00:01:15.961 --> 00:01:18.796
Concert means a show where people play music live.

26
00:01:19.096 --> 00:01:21.015
We went to a concert last night.

27
00:01:21.715 --> 00:01:24.146
Your turn. Say: Concert.

28
00:01:26.846 --> 00:01:27.708
Concert.

29
00:01:28.717 --> 00:01:29.428
Rhythm.

30
00:01:30.128 --> 00:01:32.557
Rhythm means the regular beat in music.

31
00:01:32.857 --> 00:01:34.136
Clap to the rhythm!

32
00:01:34.836 --> 00:01:37.280
Your turn. Say: Rhythm.

33
00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:40.656
Rhythm.

34
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:42.605
Song.

35
00:01:43.305 --> 00:01:45.920
Song means a short piece of music with words.

36
00:01:46.220 --> 00:01:48.010
This song is about friendship.

37
00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:51.061
Your turn. Say: Song.

38
00:01:53.761 --> 00:01:54.518
Song.

39
00:01:55.517 --> 00:01:56.367
Culture.

40
00:01:57.067 --> 00:02:00.622
Culture means the way of life, art and customs of a group of people.

41
00:02:00.922 --> 00:02:02.910
Music is part of our culture.

42
00:02:03.610 --> 00:02:05.693
Your turn. Say: Culture.

43
00:02:08.393 --> 00:02:09.360
Culture.

44
00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:12.431
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:12.731 --> 00:02:15.659
Sreypich, what kind of music do you enjoy?

46
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.275
I like pop music, such as K-pop.

47
00:02:20.583 --> 00:02:22.502
Do you like traditional music too?

48
00:02:23.817 --> 00:02:27.934
Yes! I love the roneat. It's a kind of xylophone.

49
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.774
Have you been to a concert?

50
00:02:32.083 --> 00:02:34.582
Yes, I went to a concert, and the band was great!

51
00:02:35.883 --> 00:02:38.719
Grammar focus: Kind of and such as.

52
00:02:39.019 --> 00:02:43.192
The roneat is a kind of xylophone. I like pop music, such as K-pop.

53
00:02:43.492 --> 00:02:47.236
'A kind of' explains what something is. 'Such as' gives examples.

54
00:02:48.250 --> 00:02:51.332
Now read and listen. Songs of Many Cultures.

55
00:02:51.632 --> 00:02:53.678
Every culture has its own music.

56
00:02:54.983 --> 00:02:59.549
Cambodia has traditional instruments, such as the roneat and the tro.

57
00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:04.243
Other countries have different rhythms, like samba from Brazil.

58
00:03:05.550 --> 00:03:08.943
Last month, I went to a concert and heard a great band.

59
00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.805
Music connects people, even when they speak different languages.

60
00:03:15.117 --> 00:03:17.815
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:18.115 --> 00:03:21.102
The roneat is a blank of xylophone.

62
00:03:21.402 --> 00:03:25.137
A, kind. B, such. C, type as.

63
00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:31.126
The answer is A: kind.

64
00:03:32.617 --> 00:03:34.860
I like sports, blank football and swimming.

65
00:03:35.160 --> 00:03:39.069
A, such as. B, kind of. C, because.

66
00:03:43.083 --> 00:03:45.211
The answer is A: such as.

67
00:03:46.717 --> 00:03:48.856
The regular beat in music is the blank.

68
00:03:49.156 --> 00:03:52.495
A, rhythm. B, band. C, concert.

69
00:03:56.483 --> 00:03:57.972
The answer is A: rhythm.

70
00:03:59.483 --> 00:04:03.006
Now it's your turn to speak. What kind of music do you enjoy?

71
00:04:08.306 --> 00:04:14.581
I enjoy many kinds of music, such as Khmer pop and traditional songs. My favourite instrument is the tro.

72
00:04:14.881 --> 00:04:16.846
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:04:17.850 --> 00:04:21.617
Great work today! You learned eight new words and kind of and such as.

74
00:04:21.917 --> 00:04:27.100
Today's value is cultural appreciation. Enjoy and respect the music and art of every culture.

75
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.820
See you in Unit twelve. Goodbye!

76
00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.529
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

